With just a few words, extra taps are tolerable. But as Maya's collection grows, the cumulative effort starts to obstruct the actual goal: learning the meaning and pronunciation of new words.

This matters especially in moments like this one — at home, revisiting the article, reviewing Japanese words with the clear intention of studying them. Her cognitive load is already high: she's decoding meaning, listening carefully, attempting accurate pronunciation. Any unnecessary interaction introduces avoidable friction. What begins as a minor interruption can quickly become frustration.

